{
  "id": "edit-distance",
  "questionId": "edit-distance",
  "slug": "edit-distance",
  "title": "Edit Distance",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "strings"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "define dp[i][j] as the minimum number of operations to convert the first i characters of word1 into the first j characters of word2",
    "if word1[i-1] == word2[j-1], the last characters already match and cost nothing extra: dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]",
    "if they don't match, you must pay for exactly one operation, whichever is cheapest: replace (dp[i-1][j-1]), delete from word1 (dp[i-1][j]), or insert into word1 (dp[i][j-1]), so dp[i][j] = 1 + min of those three",
    "the base cases are converting an empty prefix: dp[0][j] = j (insert j characters) and dp[i][0] = i (delete i characters)",
    "fill the table row by row and return dp[m][n]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting the base case rows/columns (converting to/from an empty string costs exactly the length of the other string)",
    "mixing up which of the three neighbors corresponds to insert versus delete versus replace",
    "adding 1 even when the characters match, instead of taking dp[i-1][j-1] directly"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `word1` and `word2`.\n\n**Find the minimum number of operations required to convert `word1` into `word2`.**\n\nIn a single operation you may insert a character, delete a character, or replace a character.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= word1.length <= 500",
      "0 <= word2.length <= 500",
      "word1 and word2 consist of lowercase English letters only"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "one or both strings are empty",
      "the two strings are already identical (zero operations needed)",
      "the two strings share no characters at all"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "word1 = \"horse\", word2 = \"ros\"",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "horse -> rorse (replace h with r) -> rose (delete r) -> ros (delete e)"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "word1 = \"intention\", word2 = \"execution\"",
        "output": "5",
        "expectedOutput": "5",
        "explanation": ""
